      "id": "p_2059eb2c",
      "title": "High Security Chaotic Encryption-based Visible Light Transmission System for UAVs",
      "abstract": "ObjectiveThe fast development of Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) systems has raised urgent demands for robust, confidential wireless data links, which has become a core research frontier in modern communications. To address the high-throughput and physical-layer security requirements of integrated air-ground networks, this work develops a Visible Light Communication (VLC) architecture tailored for UAV platforms that balances the transmission rate and information confidentiality.MethodsWe propose a secure transmission framework based on two-dimensional Chaotic Encryption Orthogonal Frequency Division Multiplexing Differential Chaos Shift Keying (CE-OFDM-DCSK). Raw user bitstreams are first mapped into two-dimensional matrices and scrambled by a 2D chaotic module. This twofold permutation exploits frequency diversity gains while reinforcing transmission secrecy. The scrambled data are subsequently modulated via a hybrid Differential Chaos Shift Keying (DCSK) and Orthogonal Frequency Division Multiplexing (OFDM) scheme to strengthen anti-interference capability. The corresponding inverse decryption and demodulation operations are implemented at the receiver side to reconstruct the original information sequence.ResultsNumerical simulations are conducted across three typical channel environments: Additive White Gaussian Noise (AWGN), multipath Rayleigh fading, and multipath VLC channels. The results demonstrate that the proposed architecture achieves stable data delivery under diverse harsh channel conditions, and outperforms mainstream benchmark systems in physical-layer security with a notable margin.ConclusionThe introduced CE-OFDM-DCSK framework embeds two-dimensional chaotic scrambling into multicarrier signal waveforms. By using frequency diversity to guarantee reliable transmission and integrating chaotic randomness for encryption, the system shows godd anti-eavesdropping performance. This work provides a viable technical solution for constructing high-reliability, secure integrated air-ground UAV visible light communication networks.",
